            <ArticleTitle>Pharmacological treatment of pain: future trends and novel insights.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>104-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/cpt.25</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The pharmacological treatment of chronic pain is generally hampered by a limited clinical outcome. Hence, there is a strong need for new therapeutic concepts considering the identification of novel targets and related drugs, but also optimization of established therapeutic regimes through individualization. In this issue, focused on &quot;Pain,&quot; we discuss some of the recent new concepts in pain treatment, understanding of pain heterogeneity, and subsequent optimization of analgesic treatment, but also novel insights into interactions of nonopioids.</AbstractText>
